And I guess one I would highlight to start with is our habit of focus, which refers to our tendency to focus on information that's right in front of us that we have easily at hand, often that someone has provided to us, and make decisions based only on that information, operating essentially under the assumption that that's all that matters or that's all there is. And one of the main ways to avoid being deceived is to think about information that people aren't showing you, or information that's missing or has been withhold or you're just not thinking about,
我想首先强调的一个习惯是我们的“关注习惯”，它指的是我们倾向于关注眼前容易获得的信息，这些信息通常是别人提供给我们的，并仅根据这些信息做出决定，本质上假设这就是全部重要内容或全部信息。避免被欺骗的主要方法之一是思考别人没有向你展示的信息，或者缺失的、被隐瞒的，或者你只是没有想到的信息，

