broadening your focus to include other information besides perhaps what the scam or a con artist wants you to be focusing on at that particular moment. So it's especially easy to fool people when you tell them something that they want to believe. anyway, or something that matches the preconceived notion. So how can we fall into the trap of not being willing to re-examine our own beliefs? This is a general issue, right, that we tend to make predictions about the world. We have to, right? We have to have expectations for what's going to happen, and we can act on those. And most of the time, that's a great thing to do. And that's true for most of these sort of cognitive tendencies. They generally work really well for us. It's only when somebody is hijacking them to take advantage of us that we run into problems. So the problem with
