but it's probably not as common as some of the biggest critics of scientific fields would want you to believe either. Most scientists that I know, and I'm sure that Dan knows and most scientists in the world, are trying to get accurate results. They're trying to report what they actually did. They're not deliberately falsifying things. But in a climate where it's reasonable to expect that scientific results that are reported are honest and true and not false, a few people can get away with inserting themselves into the process and deliberately. creating things that will then slip through and, you know, get fabricated results into the literature. I think that the general public should be skeptical of specific scientific results if they detect signs like, well, this is based on a very small sample size. It's based on a, you know,
