00:10:30.000 --> 00:11:09.000
like an investment opportunity that offers unheard of returns or a company that promises a miracle medical cure. if you're offered something that sounds like an amazing opportunity, what are the questions to ask yourself to decide if it falls into that too good to be true category? I can start with that. We all know that when something is too good to be true, we shouldn't believe it. That's something that everybody kind of knows that if it seems too good to be true, it probably is. The problem is what sounds too good to be true to one person is just good enough for another person. So for somebody else, they're going to find that as just plausible enough that they're going to jump in.
比如提供闻所未闻回报的投资机会，或者承诺奇迹般医疗治愈的公司。如果你被提供一个听起来像是绝佳机会的东西，你应该问自己什么问题来决定它是否属于“好得令人难以置信”的类别？我可以从这里开始。我们都知道，当某事好得令人难以置信时，我们不应该相信它。这是每个人都知道的事情，如果它看起来好得令人难以置信，它可能就是。问题在于，对一个人来说听起来好得令人难以置信的事情，对另一个人来说却刚刚好。所以对其他人来说，他们会觉得这足够合理，以至于他们会跳进去。

18
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:44.000
The challenge in deciding when something's too good to be true is in making sure that you view it kind of skeptically from the beginning. So if something seems really promising, really amazing, you should take a step back and say, what would I need to know in order to verify that that's actually true? We know that if somebody offers you 50% returns on your investment with a guaranteed, of no losses all within a year. Almost certainly not true because no investment does that. So you can take a step back and say, what would they have to be doing to be able to make that claim?
决定某事何时好得令人难以置信的挑战在于确保你从一开始就以怀疑的眼光看待它。所以，如果某事看起来非常有希望、非常惊人，你应该退后一步，问自己：我需要知道什么才能验证它确实是真的？我们知道，如果有人向你提供50%的投资回报，并保证一年内没有损失。这几乎肯定不是真的，因为没有任何投资能做到这一点。所以你可以退后一步，问：他们必须做什么才能做出这种声明？

