And as soon as you start questioning it a little bit, you might realize that now this really actually is too good to be true. I was just going to say, what about the case of Bernie Madoff where it was too good to be true and yet he was paying people? So you didn't really have a reason to question other than, well, the market isn't behaving this well, and yet I'm still getting 15% returns every year. I mean, how do you escape being in a situation like that? So too good to be true, as Dan said, can mean different things to different people, but there are some signs that are pretty common for things that are too good to be true,
一旦你开始稍微质疑它，你可能会意识到，不，这实际上确实好得令人难以置信。我正想说，伯尼·麦道夫的案例怎么样？那件事好得令人难以置信，但他确实在付钱给人们。所以你并没有真正的理由去质疑，除了“嗯，市场表现得没那么好，但我每年仍然能获得15%的回报”。我的意思是，你怎么能避免陷入那种情况？所以，正如丹所说，好得令人难以置信对不同的人可能意味着不同的事情，但对于那些好得令人难以置信的事情，确实有一些非常常见的迹象，

