or at least that shouldn't be believed. And in the case of Bernie Madoff, what he was offering wasn't really necessarily too good. It was not a really huge rate of return. It was 8 to 12% a year, which is a little bit above the long run average of the stock market, but not, you know, not too much. It's nothing like what an original Ponzi scheme was offering or what a lot of cryptocurrency offers the, you know, recently have offered. But the telltale sign was that it was every single year. There was never a losing year. There was barely ever even a losing month. He managed to make the returns on his investors' investments, you know, fit within that narrow band. So the excessive consistency there was, I think, what trapped people. They thought, this is a sure thing.
或者至少是不应该相信的事情。在伯尼·麦道夫的案例中，他提供的并不一定真的太好。那不是一个非常高的回报率。每年8%到12%，这比股票市场的长期平均水平高出一点点，但并没有，你知道，高出太多。这与最初的庞氏骗局所提供的，或者最近许多加密货币所提供的完全不同。但明显的迹象是，它是每年都这样。从来没有亏损的一年。甚至几乎从来没有亏损的一个月。他设法使投资者的投资回报，你知道，保持在那个狭窄的范围内。所以那里的过度一致性，我认为就是困住人们的原因。他们认为，这绝对是稳赚不赔的。

